  "text_md": "    <td>73 included in analysis (ITT)</td>\n    <td> </td>\n</table>\n  <tr>\n</table>\n  </tr>\n    <td>289 included in analysis (ITT)</td>\n    <td colspan=\"2\">215 assessed at 6 month follow-up</td>\n  <tr>\n  <tr>\n  <tr>\n  <tr>\n  </tr>\n    <td>636 excluded 202 did not meet inclusion criteria 162 declined to participate 272 other reasons</td>\n<br><br><table>\n  </tr>\n  </tr>\n  </tr>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>2 lost to follow-up 1 discontinued 1 death</td>\nIn brief, people were eligible if they were aged 18 years or older, had smoked ten or more cigarettes per day for the past year, wanted to stop smoking, and could provide consent. We recruited via community newspapers, inviting people to call the study centre for eligibility prescreening, done by research assistants, who also completed follow-up assessments. We excluded pregnant and breastfeeding women; people using cessation drugs or in an existing cessation programme; those reporting heart attack, stroke, or severe angina in the previous\n<br><br>245 assessed at 3 month follow-up<br><br><table>\n  <tr>\n  <tr>\n  </tr>\nWe did this three parallel group, randomised controlled trial in Auckland, New Zealand. First randomisation was on Sept 6, 2011, and last follow-up was on July 5, 2013. The published protocol describes procedures in detail.\n<br><br>232 assessed at 1 month follow-up<br><br><table>\n<br><br><table>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n</table>\n# Articles\n    <td colspan=\"2\"> </td>\n  <tr>\n  <tr>\n</table>\n<br><br><table>\n    <td>6 lost to follow-up 2 discontinued</td>\n</table>\n</table>\n  <tr>\n  </tr>\nFigure 1: Trial proﬁle 11 protocol violations occurred in the nicotine e-cigarettes group (three pregnancies, seven no biochemical validation, one undisclosed medication ineligibility). 11 protocol violations occurred in the patches group (four pregnancies, four no biochemical validation, three undisclosed medication ineligibility). Three protocol violations occurred in the placebo e-cigarettes group (one no biochemical validation, two undisclosed medication ineligibility). ITT=intention to treat.\n<br><br>59 assessed at 3 month follow-up<br><br><table>\n  <tr>\n### Randomisation and masking\n  <tr>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n</table>\n    <td>13 lost to follow-up</td>\n<br><br>252 assessed on quit date<br><br><table>\n  <tr>\n  <tr>\n</table>\n<br><br>62 assessed at 1 month follow-up<br><br><table>\n    <td> </td>\n  </tr>\nCallers who met the inclusion criteria and gave demographic details and information about nicotine dependence (Fagerström test for nicotine dependence [FTND]\n<br><br><table>\n  </tr>\n<br><br><table>\n    <td>295 included in analysis (ITT)</td>\n</table>\n  </tr>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n  </tr>\n    <td>8 lost to follow-up 1 discontinued</td>\n    <td>657 randomised</td>\n  <tr>",
